  "notes": "ROOT CAUSE FIX: --build-baseline idempotency bug. In scan(), the `allowed` set was always populated from existing baseline regardless of mode. This caused --build-baseline to: (1) load existing 6 entries into `allowed`, (2) skip all already-allowed matches, (3) write empty allowlist. Running check mode after would then detect 6 unallowlisted hits → exit 1. FIX: `allowed` is now mode-conditional — build-baseline uses empty Set (collects ALL current matches), check mode uses existing allowlist. VERIFICATION: (1) --build-baseline now correctly writes 6 entries; (2) idempotency confirmed — second --build-baseline also produces 6 entries; (3) check mode exit 0 with 5075 tracked files; (4) .secrets-baseline restored to correct 6 test-fixture entries (all manually verified as synthetic — not real secrets); (5) tsc --noEmit exit 0 (clean, .mjs not in tsconfig scope); (6) .github/workflows/secret-scan.yml unchanged — already correct (PR + push main/master gate). DELTA: 100% — single-line root cause fix + baseline rebuild. ADR compliance: ADR-006 (execFileSync with literal args, no user input injection).",
